From 3241ca020d78f6f161dee8ae57adc0d584e197aa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Qwen (Arena agent)" <agent@arena.local>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 06:24:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] feat(seo,auth): local-Redis correctness fix and
 discoverability baseline

Applies Revision 3 addendum sections A6 (Redis correction) and the SEO/AEO
request. A7 (MFA re-enrol) and A8 (AI chat box) were confirmed with the
user and deliberately NOT built; both are logged as Known Gaps.

A6 - local Redis as the primary store:

The Revision 2 diagnosis ("Redis is offline") was wrong. The deployment
moved from a managed provider that was rate-limiting the API to a local
instance which is live. The real defect was an uncaught store error inside
a request preHandler: rate-limit.ts called store.increment() with no error
handling, so a provider fault 500'd every rate-limited route BEFORE its
handler ran and the magic-link handler never reached app.email.send().
LoginAbuseGuard had the same uncaught pattern.

Hybrid failure policy (user decision):
- counters fail OPEN with a warn log carrying a scope, so a Redis blip
  cannot lock every user out of login
- single-use token stores fail CLOSED: MagicLinkTokenStore.issue/consume
  log and rethrow; SignupInviteCooldown suppresses the send rather than
  email-bombing an address it cannot remember emailing
- StoreLogger lives in challenge.ts (cycle-free) and app.log is now wired
  into every Redis-backed auth store; every fault is grep-able by scope
- no managed-provider limits reintroduced; REDIS_OPTIONAL stays the single
  switch and the memory shim is defence-in-depth only

Boot-probe defect found only by running against a real server:
probeRedis() called connect() whenever the method existed, but ioredis
auto-connects in its constructor and rejects connect() unless status is
"wait". The probe therefore failed against a HEALTHY server with "Redis is
already connecting/connected", silently dropping to memory mode - and in
production, where Redis is required, refusing to boot at all. connect() is
now called only from "wait". The unit-test fake implements ping alone, so
no Revision 2 test could have caught this.

New src/plugins/redis-live.test.ts proves it against real redis-server
7.0.15: single-use issue/consume, re-issue invalidation, invite cooldown
SET NX, email-window counters, fail-open counters, fail-closed token store
and invite, plus a full buildApp() boot reporting {redis:"up"} on /health.
Gated on REDIS_LIVE_URL so CI and ordinary runs skip it (9 tests).

SEO/AEO - discoverability:

lib/seo.ts is the single source of truth: robots.ts, sitemap.ts, llms.txt
and the Service graph all read one INDEXABLE_ROUTES table, so a page cannot
appear in one crawler surface and not the others.

- /robots.txt: crawl policy, sitemap advertisement, and an explicit
  AI-crawler group repeating the SAME disallows (robots groups do not
  inherit, so omitting them would have exposed /portal to exactly the
  crawlers we want answering for us). Blanket Disallow: / whenever the
  site URL is not a real public https host
- /sitemap.xml: every indexable route plus blog articles fetched
  best-effort from the content API; a partial sitemap ships rather than a
  500 when the API is down
- /llms.txt: entity brief, facts, one line per page, and the published Q&A
  re-published verbatim for retrieval engines. Nothing invented
- JSON-LD: Organization + WebSite on every page (connected via publisher),
  Service on the catalogue and its three children, BreadcrumbList on nested
  routes, Article on /blog/[slug]
- canonicals on all 15 indexable routes; /blog metadata moved to a new
  layout because the page is a client component, and /blog/[slug] overrides
  the inherited canonical
- group-level noindex on (auth), (authed) and a new checkout layout, which
  is what covers the client-component pages that cannot export metadata
- index policy keeps noindex pages CRAWLABLE: a disallowed page cannot be
  fetched, so Google never sees its noindex and may still list the bare URL

Deliberate omissions, each pinned by a test: logo (schema.org needs raster
>=112x112 and only an SVG exists), sameAs (no profiles exist in the repo and
an invented URL damages entity disambiguation), SearchAction (no site-wide
search endpoint), and FAQPage - qa-section.tsx is orphaned, so the Q&A copy
is not visibly rendered and emitting the markup would violate the
visible-content guideline. docs/seo-runbook.md carries the off-page plan.

Verification: api 1048 passed / 9 skipped, tsc clean, eslint clean; web
37 new tests, tsc clean, eslint clean, full suite 775 passed with 10
failures proven pre-existing by re-running the same five files against a
clean HEAD.
