+### Revision 3 addendum — SEO/AEO Known Gaps
+
+- **`FAQPage` markup is built and tested but NOT wired to any page.** `qa-data.ts` flags entries
+  `home: true` and its own header says the home page renders them, and `_components/home/qa-section.tsx`
+  implements exactly that — but that component is imported by no page (only by its own test), so the
+  copy is not visibly rendered anywhere. Google requires FAQ markup to match on-page content, so
+  emitting it without mounting `QaSection` would be a structured-data spam signal. The decision was
+  escalated to the user because finishing it changes the visible home page. `faqJsonLd()` is ready; the
+  two-line wiring is in `docs/seo-runbook.md`. Note also that since August 2023 Google shows FAQ rich
+  results only for well-known authoritative government and health sites, so the realistic value is
+  answer-engine grounding, not a SERP snippet.
+- **No raster organisation logo, so `Organization.logo` is omitted.** Needs a square PNG/WebP ≥112×112
+  (512×512 recommended) at e.g. `public/brand/logo-512.png`, then one line in `organisationJsonLd()`.
+- **No default Open Graph share image.** `twitter.card: 'summary_large_image'` and the OG defaults are
+  declared, but the repository ships no 1200×630 raster, so shares have no card image. `next/og`
+  (`ImageResponse`) was considered and rejected: it needs a font resolvable at runtime on Cloudflare
+  Workers, which the repo's own "no filesystem on workerd" convention argues against.
+- **`sameAs` omitted — no social/directory profiles exist in the repository.** Add the real URLs once
+  the profiles do (runbook §Off-page, step 5).
+- **Off-page work is a runbook, not code, and none of it is verified.** Search Console and Bing
+  Webmaster verification, sitemap submission, Google Business Profile, the Wikidata item, profiles and
+  link building all require accounts this sandbox has no access to. `docs/seo-runbook.md` sequences them
+  by expected return; until step 1 is done there is no crawl or query data at all.
+- **Canonical host consolidation unverified.** Canonicals are declared from `NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL`. If
+  `www` and apex are both live without a 301 to one origin, the declaration alone will not consolidate
+  them — the redirect has to be fixed at the edge first.
+- **No `hreflang`.** English only; add `alternates.languages` if a second locale ever ships (a wrong
+  `hreflang` cluster is worse than none).
+- **Ten pre-existing web test failures remain** (contributor-count drift ×3, `env.test` ×6,
+  signup-enroll ×1). Proven present on clean `HEAD` before this revision; not fixed here because
+  touching contributor data or env expectations is an unlisted change (A0.2).
